From 4794bcc0b05cfd0a71df29c2de4b7b1c49261437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kelvin Lee <kelvin.cushman@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 21:18:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(roundtable): group chat rooms for agent sessions
 with budgeted digests

Adds @bastani/roundtable: a broker-based group discussion layer where the
room transcript lives outside every session's context window. Members get
coalesced one-line activity pings; content only enters context via
deterministic, character-budgeted digests (newest verbatim, older as
headlines, rest collapsed). Read cursors are broker-side, keyed by member
name, surviving reconnects.

- broker: unix-socket room server, auto-spawned, idle shutdown (framing
  shared with @bastani/intercom)
- tool: rooms/join/leave/post/digest/peek
- extension: lazy connect, coalesced follow-up notifications
- demo: scripted 3-agent design discussion + late-joining reviewer paying
  33% of transcript cost, over the real socket
- tests: 20 (digest bound, room store, real-socket integration)
- docs: DESIGN.md, orca-integration.md, self-improvement-loop.md
